1.
| Topic                         | What it means in our project                                                                                                                                                                  |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Role-based collaboration**  | Each agent has one specific responsibility (Intake, Policy, Approval).                                                                                                                        |
| **Supervisor–Worker pattern** | The workflow/controller acts as the supervisor and delegates work to worker agents.                                                                                                           |
| **Communication channels**    | Agents pass structured information (messages/JSON) to each other.                                                                                                                             |
| **Agent isolation**           | Each agent only knows what it needs to know and doesn't perform another agent's job.                                                                                                          |
| **Event-driven agents**       | A new purchase request triggers the workflow, causing agents to run in sequence.                                                                                                              |
| **A2A (Agent2Agent)**         | One agent sends its result directly to another agent.                                                                                                                                         |
| **MCP**                       | A standard way for agents to access external tools or resources. We may not need a full MCP server for this assignment, but I'll explain where it fits and whether it should be demonstrated. |

